    description: "MEASURED 2026-11-01 in the Agda grammar A/B (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/tracker_hygiene_sweep_2026-11-01T223538Z/agda_grammar_check/cmp.py; data in cmp_stdlib.json and cmp_plfa.json). Counted: files whose parse tree holds at least one ERROR or MISSING node.\n- agda-stdlib, 1264 files: PyPI tree-sitter-agda 1.3.3 (bundled today) 571 files (45%), 2160 nodes; tree-sitter-language-pack 508 files (40%), 2064 nodes.\n- plfa, 40 files: 26 vs 23.\n\nINV-vokir (a declaration after a layout block) and WI-molon (an empty nested module body) are two named shapes. The rest is NOT CHARACTERIZED: which constructs produce the errors, and how many declarations, references and stable_ids are lost or misplaced because of them.\n\nASKED: classify the ERROR and MISSING nodes over agda-stdlib by enclosing construct (and the first token inside the error); rank the shapes by file count; for each, decide between an analyzer workaround, an upstream grammar issue, or an accepted loss, and file per-shape items. This also bears on the owner's pending grammar-swap decision (bundled 1.3.3 vs language pack; see INV-vokir and WI-molon), since both grammars share the upstream and most of the errors."  # d7b2
